WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.685
Technical OSINT is the analysis of lawfully accessible public information about

00:00:04.685 --> 00:00:06.190
internet-facing infrastructure.

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:11.185
Its sources can include domains, DNS records, internet addresses, certificates, websites,

00:00:11.185 --> 00:00:15.520
public repositories, package registries, cloud references, and technical metadata.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:17.630
The work is analytical rather than intrusive.

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:21.070
Analysts collect observable records, preserve dates and source context,

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:23.795
compare indicators, and develop cautious judgments.

00:00:23.795 --> 00:00:28.235
Technical OSINT does not authorize scanning beyond approved limits, attempting access,

00:00:28.235 --> 00:00:30.863
using exposed credentials, or bypassing controls.

00:00:30.863 --> 00:00:34.295
Defenders use technical OSINT to improve attack-surface awareness,

00:00:34.295 --> 00:00:38.950
identify unknown or stale assets, support threat intelligence, assess vendor dependencies,

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:41.110
and add public context during incidents.

00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:44.040
It can reveal questions that internal inventories should answer.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:46.080
Public records rarely tell the whole story.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:48.530
A domain may be parked, delegated, or abandoned.

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:51.220
An address may belong to a cloud provider or shared host.

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:55.360
A certificate may show that a name was validated at one time without proving current

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:56.570
ownership or security.

00:00:56.570 --> 00:00:59.410
Strong analysis separates observation from inference.

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:00.050
For example,

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:03.750
a certificate record can support that a certificate covered a hostname on a date.

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:08.030
Connecting that hostname to an organization or active system requires additional evidence

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:09.290
and confidence language.

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:11.920
The goal is responsible visibility and decision support.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:14.980
Work from an authorized scope, minimize unnecessary collection,

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:18.570
document every important source, validate across independent evidence,

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:22.240
and report risk signals as signals rather than claims of compromise.
